  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Anduril Industries reported $803M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Anduril Industries won 67 awards this fiscal year, with an average award size of $12M, and obligations are up 81.6% year over year. The Department of Homeland Security and the Department of Defense are the largest buyers, with DHS obligating $422M and DoD obligating $341M so far. Computer Systems Design Services is the largest NAICS market for Anduril Industries at $518M, followed by Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing at $222M. Historical obligations show a growth trajectory from FY21 through FY26: FY21 was $52.5M, FY22 was $211M, FY23 was $233M, FY24 was $645M, FY25 was $442M, and FY26 is $803M. Other reported markets include Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $40.1M and Aircraft Manufacturing at $20.1M. The dataset notes that figures are contract obligations except where award-value figures are marked as total contract values, and current-year totals are fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are Anduril Industries' federal obligations by agency?",
        "body": "The Department of Homeland Security and the Department of Defense account for the majority of obligations. The Department of Homeland Security obligated $422M and the Department of Defense obligated $341M in FY2026 to date. The Department of Energy obligated $40M, and other agencies make up the remainder."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which product and service markets drive Anduril Industries' federal revenue?",
        "body": "Computer Systems Design Services is the largest market at $518M, followed by Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing at $222M. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences accounted for $40.1M while Aircraft Manufacturing accounted for $20.1M. Smaller reported markets include Small Arms, Ordnance, and Ordnance Accessories Manufacturing at $3.1M and Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing at $100K."
      }
    ]
  },
